Z||000000||Cheever3000||08-21-2001||07:34 PM||||On the way home last night about half past midnight.  On the feeder road that runs alongside the toll road.  Me in my 2.8 black 88 GT, and a black 80's - early 90's Camaro happen to get ahead of the few cars that were around us.  At more than 45 mph, maybe 50 or so, he notices me and decides he wants to race.  No lights coming up, just straight flat road, so I went to 3rd and nailed it.  He pulled away VERY slowly but by the time we were done he was 1 or 1-1/2 lengths ahead.  Time for me to turn off, we flickered brights at each other.  I thought either I did well for a 2.8, or he did poorly for I guess a 3.4, or both.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Mach10||08-21-2001||07:57 PM||||I nailed a mid-80s Camaro RS last sunday. Got about 3/4 car length on him. Admittedly, this was at "Street" speeds, and we didnt' break 50kph. I'm still laughing, though...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Don't believe me? Ask BaldLobo... He was there, in the car with me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>We got a few good kills from that run  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
